NAME
       sed - stream editor

SYNOPSIS
       sed [-n] [-e script] [script] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
       Applies an editing script to every line of the input and writes
       the result to standard output.

COMMANDS
       s/re/repl/[gip]   substitute
       p                 print the current line
       d                 delete the current line
       q                 quit

ADDRESSES
       N       line number N
       $       last line
       /re/    lines matching a regular expression
       N,M     a range of lines

REPLACEMENT
       &       the whole match
       \1..\9  the corresponding capture group

OPTIONS
       -n     do not print lines automatically; only p prints
       -e S   add S to the script (repeatable)

EXAMPLES
       sed 's/foo/bar/g' in.txt
       sed -n '10,20p' log.txt

SEE ALSO
       awk(1), grep(1), tr(1)
